Fix inverted PyThread_free_lock / PyThread_release_lock in Swig::Mutex

QuickfixPython.cpp is generated with SWIG 4.2.1, which swaps these two calls
in the director Mutex class: the destructor releases the lock instead of
freeing it, and Unlock() frees it instead of releasing it.

Python 3.15 reimplements PyThread_type_lock on top of PyMutex, so releasing
an unlocked lock is now fatal. The static Director::swig_mutex_own destructor
aborts at interpreter shutdown with:

    Fatal Python error: PyMutex_Unlock: unlocking mutex that is not locked

Introduced in SWIG 21f1c923c, fixed upstream in SWIG 4.4.0 via 892be2b802
(https://github.com/swig/swig/commit/892be2b8024d391dbc78028a2e99b7800db2ea99).

--- a/C++/QuickfixPython.cpp
+++ b/C++/QuickfixPython.cpp
@@ -3446,7 +3446,7 @@
        }
 
        ~Mutex() {
-           PyThread_release_lock(mutex_);
+           PyThread_free_lock(mutex_);
        }
 
    private:
@@ -3455,7 +3455,7 @@
        }
 
        void Unlock() {
-           PyThread_free_lock(mutex_);
+           PyThread_release_lock(mutex_);
        }
 
        PyThread_type_lock mutex_;
